---
import LayoutWork from "@layouts/LayoutWork.astro";
import BadgesTech from "@components/BadgesTech.astro";
---

<LayoutWork title='Work'>
  <section class='grid'>
    <h2>ITG</h2>
    <p class='date'>Feb 2025 &mdash; Current</p>
    <BadgesTech
      techItems={[
        "React",
        "Redux",
        "TypeScript",
        "Node",
        "Tan Stack Query",
        "Zustand",
        "Jest",
        "Storybook",
        "OIDC",
        "OAuth",
      ]}
    />
    <div>
      <p>
        As part of the Land Rover Account team, develop and maintain a React
        single-page application which enables Land Rover customers to securely
        manage their contact details and marketing preferences. Built
        responsive, reusable React components, integrating with multiple REST
        APIs to deliver secure, reliable customer account functionality, with a
        focus on usability and accessibility.
      </p>
      <p>
        Led the development of a shared authentication library using
        OAuth/OpenID Connect (OIDC), creating a reusable authentication solution
        for multiple Jaguar Land Rover applications. In the absence of an
        integrated test environment, designed and built a lightweight sandbox
        application to run end-to-end tests against core authentication flows.
      </p>
      <p>
        As part of the authentication library work developed a local
        Node.js/Express based OIDC/OAuth identity provider, reducing reliance on
        third-party services, improving developer productivity, and enabling
        other teams to integrate and test authentication flows before external
        identity providers were available. Use of the local identity provider
        during development has reduced external authentication calls by an
        estimated 80%, removing the risk of rate‑limit failures. Additionally,
        as it’s running locally network responses are much faster reducing the
        time to run the E2E tests by around 70%, speeding up development.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working within a Test-Driven Development (TDD) environment, writing unit
        and integration tests to produce high-quality, maintainable code, and
        applied both BDD and TDD practices throughout the authentication
        project. Increased code coverage on legacy code in the last year by 10%
        as well as ensuring 90% unit-test coverage for all new work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2><a href='https://bikeclub.com/'>Bike Club</a></h2>
    <p class='date'>Jan 2023 &mdash; Aug 2024</p>
    <BadgesTech
      techItems={[
        "React",
        "Next.js",
        "TypeScript",
        "Jest",
        "Storybook",
        "GraphQL",
        "Dato CMS",
        "Chakra UI",
        "Shopify",
        "Liquid",
      ]}
    />
    <div class='description'>
      <p>
        Worked on the migration of the UK store from a Shopify site to a
        headless e&#8209;commerce architecture, reconstructing the UI with React
        and Next.js, retaining Shopify as the back-end.
      </p>
      <p>
        Led development of the new product pages and played a pivotal role in
        building cart, exchanges and cancellation journey, working closely with
        the UX/UI designer to deliver the new customer experience. The improved
        exchange and cancellation functionality massively reduced emails to
        customer support, and increased customer retention by 20%.
      </p>
      <p>
        Developed unit tests using Jest and React Testing Library, as well as
        maintaining components in Storybook.
      </p>
      <p>
        Provided support in code reviews and mentored junior developers within
        the team.
      </p>
      <p>
        Began working on the internationalisation of the UK site, bringing our
        sites across Europe from Shopify to one unified design system and
        codebase. This project and all frontend projects were unfortunately
        cancelled due to budget cuts, and led to me being made redundant.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2><a href='https://www.sungod.co/'>SunGod</a></h2>
    <p class='date'>Sept 2021 &mdash; Dec 2022</p>
    <BadgesTech
      techItems={["Vue", "Nuxt.js", "Tailwind CSS", "GraphQL", "Dato CMS"]}
    />
    <div>
      <p>
        Worked alongside the UX/UI designer to develop new features and updates
        for the site, major projects included overhauling the site's main
        navigation, updates to the product pages and product customiser, as well
        as revamping the “lens guide” on the product page. Utilising A/B testing
        to understand the impact of changes and optimise the user journey.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built a separate competition sub-site, utilising Nuxt and Dato, allowing
        the partnerships team to create competitions with limited to no input
        from the tech team. As part of competition site also created a system in
        Node for sending transactional emails from webhooks, which dynamically
        created HTML emails from a combination of Vue and MJML.
      </p>
      <p>
        Day-to-day maintenance of the main SunGod storefront site, working to
        resolve any bugs on the site identified from the tech team or reported
        from the wider business.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>ITG</h2>
    <p class='date'>Feb 2020 &mdash; Sept 2021</p>
    <BadgesTech
      techItems={[
        "React",
        "Framer Motion",
        "TypeScript",
        "SCSS",
        "SFMC",
        "jQuery",
      ]}
    />
    <div class='description'>
      <p>
        Created competition and offer pages for Virgin Media, including a
        "Santa's Virtual Grotto" competition which was in conjunction with
        Scope, and involved working alongside Scope’s accessibility team to
        ensure WCAG AA compliance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built seminar & webinar sign-up forms and survey sites for various
        brands across two pharmaceutical companies (Bayer and J&J) using HTML,
        SCSS, and JS in Salesforce Marketing Cloud.
      </p>
      <p>
        Developed a proof of concept for a clients in-house monthly magazine,
        built using React/Next.JS with Framer Motion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LayoutWork>
<style>
  h2 {
    a {
      &::after {
        background-image: url("/icon_arrow_outward.svg");
        background-position: center center;
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
        background-size: 100% auto;
        height: 1ch;
        width: 1.2ch;
        line-height: 1;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
